  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Preheat the oven to 220C, fan-forced, for the tortillas (see Make it yours). Thinly slice the onion. Thinly slice the cabbage with a sharp knife or mandoline. Finely chop the mint leaves, discarding the stems. Crush or finely chop the garlic.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2703460/photos/large/prep_ingredients-f4c125385266fae76e0ed991e60cb429.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pickle onion: Put 2 tbs white wine vinegar and ½ tsp sugar in a large bowl, season with salt and pepper and whisk to combine. Add the onion, toss well to combine, then set aside to pickle.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2703461/photos/large/pickle_onion-6dd028fe8b587da8d341dc98a0bc245e.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Warm tortillas: Enclose the tortillas in foil. Put in the oven for 8 mins or until softened and warmed through.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2703462/photos/large/warm_tortillas-5d0db5dc89475a917fdafbfbe8a0c665.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook chicken-style strips: Meanwhile, put the chicken-style strips, Caribbean seasoning and garlic in a bowl and turn to coat. Heat 1 tbs olive oil in a medium frypan over medium-high heat. Cook the chicken-style strips, stirring occasionally, for 5 mins or until browned and warmed through. Remove the chicken-style strips from the pan.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2703463/photos/large/cook_chicken-04133135e6882e3f0e060ba0025d7f83.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Add the cabbage, mint and 1 tbs olive oil to the pickled onion and toss well to combine. Spread the tortillas with 1½ tbs mayonnaise, then top with the slaw and chicken-style strips. Divide the tacos among plates and enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2703464/photos/large/serve_up-cb12193cbac65a37a446284cbb9c82dd.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make it yours: Don't want to turn on the oven? Put the tortillas on a plate, slightly overlapping, and microwave for 30 secs or until warmed through.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2703465/photos/large/make_it_yours-8f3b48a0190a24be488cc57a73f699c1.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
